<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 176 0 R
/E (Initially, our slope and paddle shooter design only allowed two artifacts to be shot, even though we were able to keep three in our robot at a given time. However, this was incredibly inefficient for cycling. Therefore, we iterated on our design by adding a second paddle that allowed us to shoot the last artifact. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [7 8]
>>
endobj
389 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 176 0 R
/E (Specifically, let the three artifact storing positions shown in the top image, from left to right, be numbered 1, 2, and 3, respectively. We were only able to shoot artifacts in positions 1 and 2, ending up with the initial artifact in position 3 at position 2. The second paddle brought the artifact at position 2 to position 1, so we could shoot all 3 artifacts at once.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [9]
>>
