417 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 178 0 R
/E (For our robot, our team used a flywheel, which is a spinning wheel used to launch game elements, in this case artifacts, quickly and consistently. A fast-spinning mass stores rotational energy \(angular momentum\), which transfers to the projectile when it contacts the wheel, so we needed to have a fast flywheel to make our projectiles go high and far. To find the optimal rotational speed of our flywheel, we  tested different motor powers for various distances from the target.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [9 10]
>>
endobj
418 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 178 0 R
/E (Our hardware design allowed us to utilize the turret through software to track AprilTags, so the driver can more efficiently work on other tasks. The Limelight 3A camera detects nearby tags, and, combined with odometry, provides accurate pose estimations. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [11 12]
>>
endobj
